# patch: 003-interactive-inject
# depends: 002
# generated: 2026-08-21 (against 2.1.238)
# description: Make remote_input work in the interactive Ink TTY REPL.
#              The sidecar (002) injects via StructuredIO.prependUserMessage,
#              which only the stream-json input loop drains — so injected prompts
#              never executed in interactive mode. Register globalThis
#              .__claudiverseSubmit on REPL mount, pointing at the live submit
#              handler via the submit ref. Calling it behaves exactly like the
#              local user pressing Enter: idle -> starts a turn; busy -> enqueues
#              and drains when the agent loops. SidecarClient prefers this hook
#              and falls back to prependUserMessage for stream-json sessions.
#
# ANCHOR STATUS (measured on the 2.1.238 build, 2026-08-21) — READ BEFORE BUMPING:
#   React_REPL  ANCHORED. Lands (256 uses in screens/REPL.js). Safe.
#   Sut         MINIFIED — this is `submitInputRef`, but the anchor DOES NOT LAND.
#
#   The `submitInputRef` and `handleSubmitInput` anchor rules resolve CORRECTLY
#   (verified: `anchor-dev resolve` reports `Sut -> submitInputRef` and
#   `vse -> handleSubmitInput`, both 95%) but their renames are ABSENT from the
#   built tree. Cause: both rules key on PRETTIFIED formatting — the
#   handleSubmitInput regex requires `.useRef(X);\s*` + `.current = X;` with
#   spaces — yet applyAnchorRules runs inside renamer.ts at build.sh step 2.6,
#   BEFORE prettify at step 2.7. They soft-skip during the real build and only
#   resolve when replayed against the finished tree. Rules were not touched here
#   (out of scope for this patch); fixing them is a tools-ts change.
#
#   RISK OF `Sut` IN AN ADDED LINE: if a future bundle reassigns `Sut` to some
#   other ref, this patch still APPLIES (the context line `Sut = React_REPL
#   .useRef(vse);` pins it) but __claudiverseSubmit would bind the wrong
#   function. The context line is the mitigation: it forces `Sut` to be the ref
#   initialised from the submit handler, so a silent rebind cannot pass.
#   Independently corroborated: `Sut.current(...)` is the submitter for
#   '/compact', '/rate-limit-options' and '/pro-trial-expired' in this file.
#   PROPER FIX for the next bump: make the submitInputRef anchor land (run the
#   rules post-prettify, or re-key them on unprettified text), then replace
#   `Sut` with `submitInputRef` here.
#
# STRUCTURE NOTE: in 2.1.238 `REPL` is a thin provider wrapper (jsx(i_y) inside
#   jsx(queueProvider)); the real component body is the inner `i_y`, which is
#   what the REPLComponent anchor binds. VERIFIED: the submit ref and this mount
#   effect are both inside `i_y`, so the effect runs on the real component's
#   mount, not the wrapper's.
diff --git a/screens/REPL.js b/screens/REPL.js
index d4d9456..87eef8d 100644
--- a/screens/REPL.js
+++ b/screens/REPL.js
@@ -3148,6 +3148,17 @@ ${xu}
         ),
         Sut = React_REPL.useRef(vse);
     Sut.current = vse;
+    React_REPL.useEffect(() => {
